ENGLISH
-------

Bookmaxim is an app by EmptyOne for collecting sentences from books. This policy describes what data the app processes and where it goes. In short: your quotes, notes and page photos stay on your phone.

### Data that stays on your phone

* Quotes, notes, books, colours, saved quotes, the autosuggestion and their history are stored only on your phone. The app has no accounts and no server and does not send this data anywhere.
* Page photos: the text is read on the phone (Google ML Kit on-device text recognition). Photos are never uploaded and are deleted once the quotes are saved or the screen is closed.
* A cover photo you take yourself is stored only on your phone.
* Data export creates a file when you ask for it and hands it to wherever you share it (e.g. e-mail or a drive). Nothing is exported without your action.

### Data that leaves your phone

* Book search. When you search the catalogue for a book, the text you type (title, author or ISBN) is sent to Google Books (Google LLC) and Open Library (Internet Archive) to show results and covers; covers are downloaded from them. Quotes and notes are never sent. These services handle requests under their own terms: https://policies.google.com/privacy and https://archive.org/about/terms.php. You can add a book by hand without searching.
* Google ML Kit diagnostics. The text recognition library sends Google diagnostics and usage statistics: the phone's model and OS, the app's name and version, a per-installation identifier (not meant to identify a person or device), performance metrics, image settings and size, error codes. It does not send photos or the recognised text. Data is encrypted in transit. Details: https://developers.google.com/ml-kit/android-data-disclosure

### What the app does not do

No ads, no accounts, no content analytics, no tracking. Your data is not sold or shared.

### Deleting data

Uninstalling the app or clearing its data in the phone's settings removes all of it. Single quotes, notes and books can be deleted in the app.

### Children

The app is not directed at children under 13.

### Changes

If the app starts handling data differently (e.g. an optional cloud backup), this policy and the date above will be updated.

